title: The Programme Convention
subtitle: A common manifesto must decide which unresolved argument becomes public.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: poland_party_card
view-if: month_actions < max_month_actions and poland_programme_convention_timer <= 0 and (social_floor_written = 0 or women_led_mandate = 0 or budget_breaches > 0 or early_election_risk >= 30 or opposition_list_pressure > 0)
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; poland_programme_convention_timer = 5
card-image: img/poland/cards/programme-convention.webp

= The Programme Convention

The draft contains everything: public housing, better hospitals, workplace
inspection, abortion rights, secular schools and institutional repair. It does
not contain agreement on what comes first—or what a future coalition may trade
away.

- @social_floor
- @equality_mandate
- @broad_manifesto

@social_floor
title: Make the social-democratic floor non-negotiable
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Razem and labour gain guarantees; liberals lose room.
choose-if: resources >= 1 and labor_strength + razem_strength >= 30 and labor_dissent < 65 and razem_dissent < 65
unavailable-subtitle: The plan needs one resource and a labour–Razem bloc capable of enforcing it.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; labor_credibility += 5; household_security += 2; razem_cooperation += 4; razem_dissent -= 3; budget_promises += 1; ko_relation -= 2; public_trust += 1; workers_support += 3; public_sector_support += 2; social_floor_written = 1; primary_social_slate = 1; news_headline = "The Left publishes a social floor for any coalition"

Housing, health, labour inspection and collective bargaining become dated
commitments rather than conference language. The programme is easier to trust
and harder to fit inside a liberal coalition agreement.

- #poland_card_finish

@equality_mandate
title: Put reproductive rights and equality first
subtitle: A clear generational identity, followed by a conservative counterattack.
choose-if: progressives_strength + spring_strength >= 30 and progressives_dissent < 65
unavailable-subtitle: The progressive currents are too weak or divided to bind the manifesto.
on-arrival: {!
const support = (
    Number(Q.abortion_rights_support) +
    Number(Q.lgbt_equality_support) +
    Number(Q.secular_state_support)
) / 3;
const salience = (
    Number(Q.abortion_rights_salience) +
    Number(Q.lgbt_equality_salience) +
    Number(Q.secular_state_salience)
) / 3;
const backlash = (
    Number(Q.abortion_rights_backlash) +
    Number(Q.lgbt_equality_backlash) +
    Number(Q.secular_state_backlash)
) / 3;
const raw =
    (support - 50) / 15 + salience / 55 - backlash / 60;
const net = Math.round(Math.max(
    -3,
    Math.min(3, raw * (0.45 + salience / 100))
));
const scale = Math.max(0.65, Math.min(1.50, 1 + net * 0.15));
Q.progressive_credibility += Math.max(2, Math.round(4 * scale));
Q.feminist_trust += Math.max(3, Math.round(5 * scale));
Q.progressives_dissent -= 4;
Q.spring_dissent -= 4;
Q.barons_dissent += 5 + Math.max(0, -net);
Q.psl_relation -= 3 + Math.max(0, -net);
Q.media_capacity += 1;
Q.young_support += Math.max(1, Math.round(3 * scale));
Q.women_support += Math.max(1, Math.round(3 * scale));
Q.urban_progressive_support += Math.max(1, Math.round(3 * scale));
Q.public_trust += net * 0.40;
Q.left_poll += net * 0.10;
Q.women_led_mandate = 1;
Q.primary_equality_slate = 1;
for (const issue of [
    "abortion_rights",
    "lgbt_equality",
    "secular_state"
]) {
    Q[issue + "_support"] += net >= 1 ? 2 : (net <= -2 ? -1 : 1);
    Q[issue + "_salience"] += 7;
    Q[issue + "_backlash"] += net < 0 ? 5 : 3;
}
Q.card_public_response_score = net;
Q.card_public_response = net >= 2
    ? "breakthrough"
    : (net >= 1
        ? "favourable"
        : (net <= -2
            ? "reversal"
            : (net <= -1 ? "backlash" : "contested")));
Q.public_opinion_last_issue =
    "Abortion, LGBT equality and secular schools";
Q.public_opinion_last_reception = Q.card_public_response;
Q.public_opinion_last_delta = net;
Q.public_opinion_last_action = "Programme convention: equality mandate";
Q.news_headline = net >= 1
    ? "The equality mandate matches a changing electorate"
    : (net <= -1
        ? "The equality mandate opens an immediate culture war"
        : "Equality becomes a defining test for the new Left");
!}

[? if card_public_response = "breakthrough": Legal abortion, civil equality
and secular public schools now describe a working public majority. Younger
voters hear clarity, while coalition conservatives lose the comfort of calling
the programme fringe. ?]
[? if card_public_response = "favourable": The convention's unambiguous line
lands on favourable terrain. Rural centrists resist, but the new generation
looks less isolated than the old guard predicted. ?]
[? if card_public_response = "contested": Younger voters finally hear an
unambiguous answer. Rural centrists and the party's conservative old wing hear
one too, and the country remains divided between them. ?]
[? if card_public_response = "backlash": The programme consolidates a
progressive identity inside a hostile high-attention climate. A clear mandate
also gives opponents a clear target. ?]
[? if card_public_response = "reversal": Equality and secular schooling enter
the manifesto against an explosive public mood. The Left gains definition and
loses immediate support. ?]

- #poland_card_finish

@broad_manifesto
title: Publish the broadest possible manifesto
subtitle: Immediate unity and good headlines; expensive contradictions survive.
on-arrival: party_unity += 3; left_poll += 0.2; public_trust += 1; barons_dissent -= 1; spring_dissent -= 1; labor_dissent -= 1; progressives_dissent -= 1; razem_dissent += 2; budget_breaches += 1; turnout_readiness += 1; primary_cross_faction_pact = 1; primary_rules_written = 1; news_headline = "Everyone finds a promise in the Left manifesto"

Every caucus gets its paragraph and nobody has to rank the promises. The launch
is peaceful. The first budget negotiation will reveal that avoiding a decision
is also a decision.

- #poland_card_finish
